  "notes": "JAPANESE AQUACULTURE:\nJapan is a major aquaculture producer, especially for:\n- {鮭|さけ}/サーモン - salmon\n- {鯛|たい} - sea bream\n- {牡蠣|かき} - oysters\n- {海苔|のり} - seaweed/nori\n- うなぎ - eel\n- {鮪|まぐろ} - tuna (recent developments)\n- ホタテ - scallops\n\nPEARL CULTIVATION:\n{養殖|ようしょく}{真珠|しんじゅ} (cultured pearls) were pioneered by {御木本|みきもと}{幸吉|こうきち} (Mikimoto Kokichi) in Japan.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {天然|てんねん} - wild-caught, natural\n- {天然|てんねん}{物|もの} - wild-caught (product)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {養殖|ようしょく}{業|ぎょう} - aquaculture industry\n- {養殖|ようしょく}{場|じょう} - fish farm\n- {養殖|ようしょく}{魚|ぎょ} - farmed fish",
